     <td>yes</td></tr>
 <tr><td><tt>powerSort()</tt></td>
     <td>\f$ O( n + n H ) \f$</td><td>\f$ O( n + n H ) \f$</td>
     <td>\f$ O( n ) \f$</td><td>yes</td></tr>
 <tr><td><tt>quickSort()</tt></td><td>\f$ \Theta( n^2 ) \f$</td>
     <td>\f$ 1.386 \, n \log_2 n \f$</td><td>\f$ O( n ) \f$ stack</td>
     <td>no</td></tr>
 <tr><td><tt>pdqSort()</tt>, <tt>vectorQuickSort()</tt></td>
     <td>\f$ O( n \log n ) \f$</td>
     <td>\f$ O( n \log n ) \f$, \f$ O( n \log k ) \f$ for \f$ k \f$
     keys (<tt>pdqSort()</tt>, <tt>vectorQuickSort()</tt>)</td>
     <td>\f$ O( \log n ) \f$ stack</td><td>no</td></tr>
 <tr><td><tt>sampleSort()</tt></td><td>\f$ O( n \log n ) \f$</td>
     <td>\f$ n \log_2 n + O( n ) \f$</td>
     <td>\f$ O( k b ) \f$ items, blocks of \f$ b \f$</td><td>no</td></tr>
 <tr><td><tt>learnedSort()</tt></td><td>\f$ O( n \log n ) \f$, by
     <tt>sampleSort()</tt> when the model does not fit</td>
     <td>\f$ O( n \log( n / k ) ) \f$ when it fits</td>
     <td>\f$ \Theta( n ) \f$</td><td>no</td></tr>
 <tr><td><tt>heapsort()</tt></td><td>\f$ O( n \log n ) \f$</td>
     <td>\f$ O( n \log n ) \f$</td><td>\f$ O( 1 ) \f$</td><td>no</td></tr>
 <tr><td><tt>countingSort()</tt></td><td>\f$ \Theta( n + k ) \f$</td>
     <td>\f$ \Theta( n + k ) \f$</td><td>\f$ \Theta( k ) \f$</td>
     <td>not applicable</td></tr>
 <tr><td><tt>radixSort()</tt></td><td>\f$ O( w ( n + 256 ) ) \f$</td>
     <td>\f$ O( w ( n + 256 ) ) \f$</td><td>\f$ \Theta( n ) \f$</td>
     <td>yes</td></tr>
 <tr><td><tt>msdRadixSort()</tt></td><td>\f$ O( D + n \log \sigma ) \f$</td>
     <td>\f$ O( D + n \log \sigma ) \f$</td><td>\f$ \Theta( n ) \f$</td>
     <td>not applicable</td></tr>
 </table>

 The bounds of the table are in comparisons for the sorts by comparisons and
 in time for the others; the stability is not applicable where equal items
 cannot be told apart (integers, strings).

